{"id": "wwdc2019-722", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/722", "wordCount": 3171, "segments": [{"start": 15.0, "text": "Hello. Thank you."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "My name is Tony Parker, I'm the"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "manager of the Foundation Team"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "at Apple, and today I'm excited"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "to have the privilege to"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "introduce you to our newest"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "It's called Combine."}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "Let's talk about asynchronous"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "programing."}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "Here I have an app that I'm"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "working on that allows students"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "to sign up for my brand-new"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "wizarding school."}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "And as you can see, it's got"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "some pretty simple requirements."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "First, we need to have a valid"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "username which we're going to"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "check by making a network"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "request to our server."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "We also need of course to have"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "matching passwords which is"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "something that we can check"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "locally in the app."}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "And while we do all of these"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "things, of course we need to"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "maintain a responsive user"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "interface, not blocking the main"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "thread."}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "So let's try using it and see"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "how this works."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "First, I'm going to start typing"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "the username like, I don't know."}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "How about Merlin."}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "Seems like a pretty good wizard"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "name. And already there's plenty of"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "asynchronous behaviors going on."}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "I used Target/Action to listen"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "for notifications about the user"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "typing."}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "I use a timer to wait for the"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "user to stop typing just for a"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "little bit so I don't overwhelm"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "my server with network requests."}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "And finally, I use something"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "like KVO to listen for progress"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "updates about that asynchronous"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "operation."}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "Now if we continue, we'll find"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "out that we get a response from"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "that request and we have to"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "update our UI."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "So I pick a new username and"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "then my super-secret secure"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "password of 12345."}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "Please don't use that password,"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "just for demo purposes."}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "But here now we've done a lot"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "more asynchronous work."}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "We had to wait for the response"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "for our URL session request."}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "We had to merge that result with"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "the result of our synchronous"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "checking and finally I had to do"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "all of those things -- once all"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "of those things were completed,"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "I had to update my UI again"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "using something like KVC."}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "So across the Cocoa SDK you'll"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "find plenty of asynchronous"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "interfaces."}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "Some you saw here like"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "Target/Action, but there's a lot"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "more, including"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "NotificationCenter and lots of"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "ad-hoc callbacks."}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "These are API's that take a"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "closure or completion block."}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "All of these things have"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "important and different use"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "cases."}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "But sometimes when you need to"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "compose them together, it can be"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "a little bit challenging."}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "So with Combine we set out not"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "to replace all of these but"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "instead to find what was common"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "amongst them."}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "And that's what Combine is, a"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "unified declarative API for"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "processing values over time."}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "Combine is written in and for"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "Swift."}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "That means we can take advantage"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "of Swift features like Generics."}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "Generics let us reduce the"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "amount of boilerplate code that"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "you need to write."}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "It also means that we can write"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "generic algorithms about"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "asynchronous behaviors once and"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "have them apply to all kinds of"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "different asynchronous interfaces."}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "Combine is also type safe,"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "allowing us to catch errors at"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "compile time instead of at"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "runtime. Our main design point about"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "Combine is that it is"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "composition first."}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "What that means is that the core"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "concepts are simple and easy to"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "understand, but when you put"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "them together, you can make"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "something that's more than the"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "sum of its parts."}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "And finally, Combine is"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "request-driven, allowing you the"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "opportunity to more carefully"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "manage the memory usage and"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "performance of your app."}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "So let's talk about those key"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "concepts. There's only three: Publishers,"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "Subscribers and Operators."}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "And we'll go over each in turn."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "First, Publishers."}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "Publishers are the declarative"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "part of Combine's API."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "They describe how values and"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "errors are produced."}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "They're not necessarily the"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "thing that actually produces"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "them."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "That means as descriptions, they"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "are value types which in Swift"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "means we use a struct."}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "Publishers also allow for"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "registration of a Subscriber;"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "that will be something that"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "receives these values over time."}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "Here's the protocol."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "It's called Publisher."}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "It has two associated types: the"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "Output, that's the kind of value"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "that it produces, and the"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "Failure which is the kind of"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "errors that it produces."}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "If it's not possible for a"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "Publisher to produce an error,"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "then you can use the type never"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "for that associated type."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "Publisher has one key function."}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "It's called Subscribe."}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "As you can tell from the generic"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "constraints on this function,"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "Subscribe requires the"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "Subscriber's Input to match the"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "Publisher's Output, and the"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "Subscriber's Failure to match"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "the Publisher's Failure."}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "Here's an example of a"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "Publisher."}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "This is our new Publisher for"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "NotificationCenter."}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "As you can see, it's a struct"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "and its Output type is"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "Notifications and its Failure"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "type is Never."}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "It is initialized with three"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "things, which center, which name"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "and which object."}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "If you're familiar with our"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "existing NotificationCenter API,"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "they should look very familiar."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "So again, we're not replacing"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "NotificationCenter."}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "We're just adapting it."}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "Next, Subscribers."}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "Subscribers are the counterpart"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "to Publishers."}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "They are what receive values,"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "including the completion if the"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "Publisher is finite."}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "Because Subscribers usually act"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "and mutate state upon receipt of"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "values, we use reference types"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "in Swift which means they are"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "classes."}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "Here's the protocol for"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "Subscriber."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "As you can see, it has the same"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "two associated types: Input and"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "Failure. Again, if the Subscriber is"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "unable to receive Failures, then"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "you can use the type Never."}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "And three key functions."}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "It can receive a subscription."}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "A subscription is how a"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "Subscriber controls the flow of"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "data from a Publisher to a"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "Subscriber."}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "It can also of course receive"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "Input. And finally, if the Publisher"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "that it is connected to is"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "finite, then it can receive a"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "Completion which can be either"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "Finished or Failure."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "Here is an example Subscriber."}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "This one is called Assign."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "Assign is a class and it's"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "initialized with an instance of"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "a class, an instance of an"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "object and a type safe key path"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "into that object."}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "What it does is when it receives"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "input, it writes it out to that"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "property on that object."}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "Because in Swift there's no way"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "to handle an error when you're"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "just writing a property value,"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "we set the failure type of"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "Assign to Never."}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "Let's talk about how these fit"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "together."}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "So you may have some kind of"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "controller object or other type"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "which holds your Subscriber, and"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "that will be responsible for"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "calling Subscribe with the"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "Subscriber to the Publisher,"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "attaching it."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "At that point, the Publisher"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "will send a subscription to the"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "Subscriber which the Subscriber"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "will use to make a request from"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "the Publisher for a certain"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "number of values or unlimited."}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "At that point, the Publisher is"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "free to send that number of"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "values or less to the"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "Subscriber."}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "And again, if the Publisher is"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "finite, then it will eventually"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "send a Completion or an Error."}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "So again, one subscription, zero"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "or more values and a single"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "Completion."}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "So returning to our example,"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "let's say that I have a model"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "object called Wizard and all I"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "care about today is what grade"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "that wizard is in."}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "Let's start with Merlin who is"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "currently in fifth grade."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "What I want to do is listen for"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "a notification about my students"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "graduating, and once they've"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "graduated, I want to update my"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "model object's value."}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "So I start with a"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "NotificationCenter Publisher on"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "the default center about"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "graduation of Merlin."}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "Next, I create an Assign"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "Subscriber and tell it to write"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "the new grade to Merlin's grade"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "property."}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "Next, I can use Subscribe to"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "attach them."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "However, as you might expect,"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "this doesn't compile."}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "And the reason is because the"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "types don't match."}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "NotificationCenter makes"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "notifications but Assign being"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "configured to write to an"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "integer property expects an"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "integer."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "So what we need is something in"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "the middle to convert between"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "notifications and integers."}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "What that is, is an Operator."}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "Operators are Publishers until"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "they adopt the Publisher"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "protocol."}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "And they are also declarative"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "and therefore value types."}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "What they do is describe a"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "behavior for changing values,"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "adding values, removing values"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "or any number of different kinds"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "of behaviors."}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "And subscribe to another"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "Publisher which we call the"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "upstream, and send the result to"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "a Subscriber, which we call the"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "downstream. Here is an example of an"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "Operator."}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "This one is one that you'll"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "become very familiar with when"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "you use Combine."}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "It's called Map."}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "Map is a struct that is"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "initialized with which upstream"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "it connects to and how to"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "convert its upstream's output"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "into its own output."}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "Because Map doesn't generate"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "Failures of its own, it simply"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "mirrors its upstream's Failure"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "type and it will just pass it"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "through."}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "So with Map we have the tool we"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "need to convert between"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "notifications and integers."}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "Let's see how."}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "So keeping the same Publisher"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "and Subscriber and before, I'm"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "adding this converter which as"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "you can see is configured to"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "connect to the"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "graduationPublisher and has a"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "closure."}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "That closure receives a"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "notification and looks for a"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "user info key called NewGrade."}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "If it's there, and if it's an"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "integer, then we return it from"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "this closure."}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "If it's not there, or if it's"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "not an integer, the new use a"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "default value of zero."}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "What that means is that no"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "matter what, the result of this"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "closure is an integer and"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "therefore I can connect this to"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "the Subscriber."}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "And everything connects,"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "compiles and works."}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "Now all of this construction"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "syntax can get a bit verbose, so"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "we also have a more fluent"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "syntax."}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "Here's how it works."}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "As an extension on the Publisher"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "protocol, meaning it's available"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "to all Publishers, we added a"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "series of functions named after"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "each Operator."}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "Here is the one for Map."}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "As you can see, its arguments"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "are everything needed to"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "initialize a Map except for"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "upstream."}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "And the reason is because as an"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "extension on Publisher we can"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "simply use self."}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "Now this may seem like a pretty"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "trivial convenience, but"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "actually this is what's really"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "going to transform how you think"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "about asynchronous programing in"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "your app."}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "Let's return to our example but"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "use the new syntax."}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "So here I am starting with the"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "NotificationCenter Publisher for"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "graduated on Merlin."}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "Once I receive a notification, I"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "then map it using the same"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "closure as we saw earlier, and"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "then I assign it to the grade"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "property on Merlin."}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "And you can see this syntax"}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "provides a very linear,"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "easy-to-understand flow of what"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "happens step-by-step."}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "Assign returns something called"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "a cancelable."}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "Cancelation is also built into"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "combine."}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "Cancelation allows you to tear"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "down the sequence of Publishers"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "and Subscribers early if you"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "need to."}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "So this step-by-step syntax is"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "really the heart of how you use"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "Combine."}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "Each step describes the next set"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "of instructions in a chain."}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "Transforming values as they make"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "their way from the first"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "Publisher through a series of"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "Operators and ending in a"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "Subscriber."}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "And we have a lot of these"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "Operators."}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "We call them our Declarative"}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "Operator API."}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "They include functional"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "transformations like Map."}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "We also have Filter and Reduce,"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "list operations like taking the"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "first, second or fifth element"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "of the Publisher."}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "Error handling like turning an"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "error into a default or"}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "placement value."}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "Thread or Q Movement, for"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "example moving heavy processing"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "work to a background thread or"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "UI work to the main thread."}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "And scheduling and time,"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "including integration with from"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "loop, dispatch queue, support"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "for timer, timeouts and more."}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "And with so many of these"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "operators available, it can be"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "perhaps a bit overwhelming to"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "think about how you will"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "navigate amongst these."}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "So what I encourage you to do is"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "return to our core design"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "principle about Combine, and"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "that is composition."}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "Instead of providing a few"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "operators that do a lot, we"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "provide a lot of operators that"}, {"start": 709.0, "text": "just do a little bit each,"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "making them easier to"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "understand."}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "So to help you navigate amongst"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "all these operators, we drew"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "inspiration for their names from"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "the existing Swift Collection"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "APIs."}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "Here's how."}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "Let's imagine a quadrant graph."}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "So on one side I have"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "synchronous APIs and the other"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "asynchronous."}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "On the top I have single values"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "and on the bottom I have many"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "values."}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "So in Swift, if you need to"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "represent an integer"}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "synchronously, you might use"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "something like int."}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "If you need to represent many"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "integers synchronously, you"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "would use something like an"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "array of integers."}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "In Combine we took these"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "concepts and mapped them into"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "the asynchronous world."}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "So if you need to represent a"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "single value asynchronously, it"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "comes later, we have a future."}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "If you need to represent many"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "values asynchronously, that's a"}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "Publisher."}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "So what that means is that if"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "you're looking for a particular"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "kind of operation that you"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "already know how to do with an"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "array, try using that name on a"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "Publisher."}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "Let me show you an example."}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "So here I chose to use a default"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "value of zero if the key was not"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "present or if it was not an"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "integer."}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "Maybe instead it would be a"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "better idea to not allow this"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "bad value to progress and end up"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "written into my model object."}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "So one thing I could do is allow"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "this closure to return nil and"}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "then filter out the nil values."}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "Well, in Swift 4.1, the standard"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "library introduced a name for"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "that operation."}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "It's called compactMap."}, {"start": 796.0, "text": "And so Publisher has one too."}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "And it behaves in a very similar"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "way."}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "If you return nil from this"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "closure, then compactMap will"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "filter it out, keeping it from"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "progressing further down the"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "stream."}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "Let's build up our step-by-step"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "instructions using a few more"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "familiar names."}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "Let's say that only students in"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "fifth grade or higher are"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "allowed in my school."}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "I can do that using Filter."}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "Filter takes a predicate and"}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "only allows elements that pass"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "that predicate to proceed."}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "This is exactly the same"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "behavior as Filter on Array."}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "Let's say furthermore that"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "you're only allowed to graduate"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "a maximum of three times."}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "So on Array, if you need to take"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "the first three elements, you"}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "could use prefix 3."}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "On a Publisher, if you want to"}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "receive the first three elements"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "only, you can use prefix of 3."}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "What it does is after it"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "receives three values, it will"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "Cancel the upstream and send a"}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "Completion to the downstream."}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "So stepping back, let's see what"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "we have here."}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "We have a NotificationCenter"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "Publisher that listens for"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "graduations on Merlin."}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "Once he graduates, we will fetch"}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "the NewGrade out of that"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "property, out of that"}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "Notification."}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "And then we will make sure that"}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "the value is greater than fifth"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "grade and that it has only"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "happened a maximum of three"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "times before finally assigning"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "it to the grade property on"}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "Merlin."}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "Now Map and Filter are great"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "APIs but they're primarily for"}, {"start": 878.0, "text": "synchronous behaviors."}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "Combine really starts to shine"}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "when you're working in"}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "asynchronous world."}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "So here are two more operators"}, {"start": 885.0, "text": "that I'm going to talk about"}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "that can be really useful for"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "that."}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "First, Zip."}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "So let's say in my app before"}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "the user is allowed to continue,"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "they need to wait for their wand"}, {"start": 895.0, "text": "to be created which is three"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "long-running asynchronous"}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "operations like this."}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "So the Continue button becomes"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "enabled once all three things"}, {"start": 904.0, "text": "are finished."}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "This is a job for Zip."}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "Zip converts several upstream"}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "inputs into a single tuple."}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "Because it requires input from"}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "all of its upstreams in order to"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "proceed, it makes it a kind of"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "when/and operation as in, when"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "this and this and this have"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "finished, do this other thing."}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "So for example, my first"}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "Publisher produces A, and then"}, {"start": 927.0, "text": "when my second Publisher"}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "produces a 1, I now have enough"}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "information to create a tuple"}, {"start": 932.0, "text": "and send that value downstream"}, {"start": 934.0, "text": "to my Subscriber."}, {"start": 937.0, "text": "In my app, I use the version of"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "Zip that takes three upstreams"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "to await the result of three"}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "asynchronous operations that"}, {"start": 944.0, "text": "each give me a Boolean result."}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "So I map the tuple into a single"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "Boolean and here I've written it"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "into the isEnabled property on"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "the button to turn it on."}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "So after you're done waiting for"}, {"start": 956.0, "text": "your wand to be created, like"}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "everybody else, my students have"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "to agree to a set of terms and"}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "conditions before they are"}, {"start": 962.0, "text": "allowed to proceed to playing"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "with their wands."}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "What that means is that all"}, {"start": 966.0, "text": "three of these switches have to"}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "be enabled before the Play"}, {"start": 969.0, "text": "button is enabled."}, {"start": 970.0, "text": "However, if one of them is then"}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "later disabled, we need to"}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "disable the button."}, {"start": 975.0, "text": "This is a job for Combine"}, {"start": 977.0, "text": "Latest."}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "Like Zip, it converts several"}, {"start": 979.0, "text": "upstream inputs into a single"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "value."}, {"start": 982.0, "text": "However, unlike Zip, it requires"}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "an input from any of its"}, {"start": 985.0, "text": "upstreams to proceed, making it"}, {"start": 987.0, "text": "a kind of when/or operation."}, {"start": 989.0, "text": "In order to support that, it"}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "stores the last value that it's"}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "received from each upstream."}, {"start": 994.0, "text": "And it's also configured with a"}, {"start": 995.0, "text": "closure that lets you convert"}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "that into a single downstream"}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "value."}, {"start": 999.0, "text": "So for example, when my first"}, {"start": 1001.0, "text": "Publisher produces A, and my"}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "second Publisher produces A1, I"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "then run my closure which"}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "stringifies this and sends it"}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "downstream."}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "Later, when the second Publisher"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "produces a new value, I can"}, {"start": 1013.0, "text": "combine it with the value from"}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "previously from the first"}, {"start": 1016.0, "text": "Publisher and send that new"}, {"start": 1018.0, "text": "value down."}, {"start": 1019.0, "text": "That means that I get new events"}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "as any upstream changes."}, {"start": 1024.0, "text": "So in my example app, I used a"}, {"start": 1026.0, "text": "version of CombineLatest which"}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "takes three upstreams, the"}, {"start": 1029.0, "text": "Boolean states of all three of"}, {"start": 1031.0, "text": "those switches as they change,"}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "convert them into a single"}, {"start": 1034.0, "text": "Boolean value again and write"}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "that to the isEnabled property"}, {"start": 1037.0, "text": "on my Play button."}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "That means that if any of them"}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "are false, the result is false."}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "But if all of them are true,"}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "then the result is true, thus"}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "enabling the button."}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "So we designed Combine to be"}, {"start": 1050.0, "text": "adoptable incrementally in your"}, {"start": 1051.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "You don't have to convert everything over to use this."}, {"start": 1054.0, "text": "So to get started, I have a few"}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "suggestions on places that you"}, {"start": 1057.0, "text": "might find in your app today"}, {"start": 1059.0, "text": "that you can use Combine for."}, {"start": 1061.0, "text": "For example, if you use"}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "NotificationCenter, you receive"}, {"start": 1064.0, "text": "notifications and then you look"}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "inside them to decide whether to"}, {"start": 1067.0, "text": "act or not, try using Filter."}, {"start": 1070.0, "text": "If you weight the result of"}, {"start": 1072.0, "text": "several asynchronous operations,"}, {"start": 1074.0, "text": "then you can use Zip, including"}, {"start": 1077.0, "text": "network operations."}, {"start": 1079.0, "text": "And finally, if you use URL"}, {"start": 1082.0, "text": "Session to receive some data and"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "then you convert that data into"}, {"start": 1085.0, "text": "your own objects using JSON"}, {"start": 1086.0, "text": "Decoder, we have an operator"}, {"start": 1088.0, "text": "that will help with that as"}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "well. It's called Decode."}, {"start": 1093.0, "text": "So we went over the basics"}, {"start": 1095.0, "text": "today. Publishers, Subscribers and"}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "Operators."}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "However, there's a lot more to"}, {"start": 1099.0, "text": "Combine."}, {"start": 1100.0, "text": "And that includes error handling"}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "and cancelation, schedulers and"}, {"start": 1104.0, "text": "time, and some great design"}, {"start": 1106.0, "text": "patterns including using Combine"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "in different modules or between"}, {"start": 1110.0, "text": "different areas of your app."}, {"start": 1111.0, "text": "And of course integration with"}, {"start": 1113.0, "text": "SwiftUI. For more on that, please watch"}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "Combine In Practice."}, {"start": 1119.0, "text": "That's all I have today."}]}